&#8220;Thank you Old Navy for holding me down. In high school, I used to steal from you guys all the time. So it&#8217;s just a full-circle moment that I&#8217;m an ambassador for Old Navy,&#8221; she said during an Instagram Live on Wednesday (Aug. 12). &#8220;I used to steal all the time and I never got caught. If it wasn&#8217;t for you guys, I probably wasn&#8217;t the freshest bi&#8211;h in school.&#8221;

Cardi complimented Old Navy&#8217;s fit and denim cut, as the shape of the company&#8217;s jeans is BBL-friendly, unlike many denim brands she&#8217;s tried over the years.

&#8220;BBL bi&#8211;hes, it is so hard for us to find jeans. Chanel and the stuff like that, we can&#8217;t wear those types of jeans. The only big brand that kind of fit our bodies are Acme Studios,&#8221; Cardi explained. &#8220;This is the type of body I have, I&#8217;m 5&#8217;3&#8243; and I&#8217;m skinny, I got no waist, but my ass and hips is the size of Uganda. They don&#8217;t make jeans for a bi&#8211;h like me.&#8221;

As the face of the fall campaign, Cardi starred in a Western-themed The Most Wanted ad alongside Wisdom Kaye and Quen Blackwell, which arrived Aug. 4. The high-waisted cuffed jeans Cardi&#8217;s sporting in the campaign are available in seven colorways on Old Navy&#8217;s website for $49.99.

“When you have a BBL it’s hard to find jeans… but Old Navy got everything for everybody,” she wrote on X in support of becoming an Old Navy ambassador.

Cardi returned to release her first single of 2026 with&nbsp; “Ah Ha ,&#8221; which debuted at No. 25 on the Billboard Hot 100. The 33-year-old Bronx native earned her fourth diamond song after the RIAA certified the Billboard Hot 100 -topping&nbsp; “WAP” earlier in August.
